WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:04.440
Recovery restores trusted operations after containment and eradication have reduced the

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:05.990
risk to an acceptable level.

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:10.205
Recovery may include rebuilding systems, restoring from backups, re-enabling services,

00:00:10.205 --> 00:00:12.600
validating patches, checking data integrity,

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.095
reviewing account state, and monitoring for recurrence.

00:00:15.095 --> 00:00:17.125
The phrase trusted operations is important.

00:00:17.125 --> 00:00:20.925
Recovery should not mean turning everything back on as quickly as possible and hoping the

00:00:20.925 --> 00:00:21.595
issue is gone.

00:00:21.595 --> 00:00:25.330
It means the organization has enough evidence that systems are safe to operate,

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:26.330
controls are working,

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:29.005
and business owners understand any residual risk.

00:00:29.005 --> 00:00:30.270
Recovery is usually coordinated,

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:33.600
because technical readiness and business readiness are not always the same.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.940
A system owner may confirm that a server is rebuilt,

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:39.130
while a business owner confirms that a process can resume.

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:43.235
Monitoring should continue after recovery because some issues reappear only after normal

00:00:43.235 --> 00:00:44.575
traffic returns.

00:00:44.575 --> 00:00:47.925
Communication also matters: stakeholders need to know what is restored,

00:00:47.925 --> 00:00:50.100
what remains limited, what users should expect,

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.595
and when the next update will come.

00:00:51.595 --> 00:00:55.330
Good recovery closes the immediate incident while keeping watch for signs that more work

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:56.095
is needed.

00:00:56.095 --> 00:00:58.700
Recovery should include a deliberate observation period.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:02.500
After service is restored, responders should keep watching relevant logs, alerts,

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:04.400
account behavior, and business signals.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:08.235
That follow-up monitoring helps confirm that eradication worked and gives stakeholders

00:01:08.235 --> 00:01:10.995
confidence that normal operations are returning for the right

00:01:10.995 --> 00:01:11.600
reasons.
